WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.525
Every Allen quarry has a posted Emergency Contacts

00:07.525 --> 00:10.237
sheet, and the same information is on your site's

00:10.237 --> 00:13.075
page on the Allen training site, where every number

00:13.075 --> 00:15.463
is tap-to-call. This video walks you through how

00:15.463 --> 00:16.387
to use it.

00:17.521 --> 00:21.333
Step one for any serious injury, fire or emergency:

00:21.333 --> 00:25.208
call 911. The card tells you exactly what to say:

00:25.208 --> 00:27.471
the site name and address, and where the injured

00:27.471 --> 00:30.646
person is, underground, pit, plant,

00:30.646 --> 00:34.071
scale or shop. Stay on the line and do what dispatch

00:34.071 --> 00:36.696
tells you. Any miner can make that call.

00:36.696 --> 00:39.170
If the injured person is underground,

00:39.170 --> 00:41.933
any miner can meet the ambulance at the portal,

00:41.933 --> 00:44.096
and the injured person comes out by the primary

00:44.096 --> 00:45.145
escapeway.

00:46.291 --> 00:49.516
Step two: call mine command, starting at the top

00:49.516 --> 00:52.341
of the list for your site, until you reach someone.

00:52.341 --> 00:54.978
Hunter Kenney is over all of our sites.

00:54.978 --> 00:58.403
At Boonesboro, it's Dustin Conn and Kendell Barnes.

00:58.403 --> 01:01.678
At Dix River, Gene Smith and Braden Walters.

01:01.678 --> 01:05.215
At Clover Bottom, Andrew Burton and Braden Walters.

01:05.215 --> 01:07.178
Their numbers are on your card. They'll send a

01:07.178 --> 01:09.578
person to meet the ambulance and they'll make the

01:09.578 --> 01:11.416
required notifications.

01:12.578 --> 01:15.328
For a death, an injury that could cause death,

01:15.328 --> 01:18.078
an entrapment, or other serious accidents,

01:18.078 --> 01:21.703
the company must notify MSHA within 15 minutes.

01:21.703 --> 01:23.878
That's the job of mine management, but you should

01:23.878 --> 01:26.428
know it exists, so tell them right away.

01:27.546 --> 01:30.246
The card also lists mine rescue. For all of our

01:30.246 --> 01:33.071
sites, that's the Kentucky Division of Mine Safety's

01:33.071 --> 01:35.946
Crestwood and Hazard mine rescue stations.

01:35.946 --> 01:38.334
It lists the Kentucky mine safety office,

01:38.334 --> 01:41.971
MSHA, and explosives contacts. Management uses

01:41.971 --> 01:45.071
these, but knowing they're there helps in an emergency.

01:46.250 --> 01:48.913
Finally, the card shows the nearest hospitals with

01:48.913 --> 01:51.788
directions, and your site's gathering points.

01:51.788 --> 01:54.838
At Boonesboro, it's the tag board or the area behind

01:54.838 --> 01:57.688
the mine outside the 22 North escapeway.

01:57.688 --> 02:00.800
At Dix River, the tag board. At Clover Bottom,

02:00.800 --> 02:03.088
the tag board, the old mine entrance,

02:03.088 --> 02:05.538
or behind the mine at the haul road to the asphalt

02:05.538 --> 02:06.326
plant.

02:07.446 --> 02:10.721
911 first, say where you are and where the injured

02:10.721 --> 02:13.671
person is, then mine command. Know your gathering

02:13.671 --> 02:15.708
point. Keep the card handy.

02:16.824 --> 02:19.986
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

02:19.986 --> 02:21.487
override this video.
